# Session buffer

Target file: `journal/session-buffer.md`

## When to append

At the **end of a turn** that produced meaningful progress, append **one** short entry:

- Repo edits, new or updated study materials
- Strategy decisions worth tracking
- Practice outcomes worth tracking (e.g. mock results, weak-area notes)

## When to skip

Do **not** append for:

- Pure clarifications or Q&A with no durable outcome
- Failed or aborted work
- Turns that only read files or planned without changing anything
- Diary consolidation itself (handled by the diary rule)

## Format

- Persist in **English**
- High-level actions only — not chat transcripts or full Q&A
- Bullets, not paragraphs; do not invent progress
- Append at the end of the file (keep the purpose header)

```markdown
### YYYY-MM-DD — short label
- Area: project | study (verbal/numerical/spatial) | process
- Done: …
- Evolved: … (vs prior state, if clear)
- Next (optional): …
```

## Do not

- Dump verbatim questions and answers
- Duplicate the same turn under multiple headings
- Edit or rewrite older buffer entries unless fixing a clear mistake
- Write diary entries here — use `journal/diary.md` only via the diary rule when the user asks
